       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so the effects could last a long time. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify going above that limit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for frail or elderly patients or those with hepatic impairment\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, give me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
